// C and Python join adjacent string literals; Ziman does not. `"one " "two"` is two statements,
// and the second is thrown away -- so the value is silently half of what was written, which is the
// worst shape a wrong answer can take. The fix is a backslash at the end of the first line.
fn main() {
    val greeting = "one " "two"
    print(greeting)
}
